node_modules/
dist/
build/
.env
.env.local
*.log
coverage/

# The local document store (STORAGE_PATH). Both paths are anchored, and both
# are needed: STORAGE_PATH defaults to ./storage, so the store lands beside
# whichever directory the process was started from — the repository root for
# `npm run dev:api`, and apps/api when the workspace is run directly. Only the
# root one was listed, so running the API from its own directory left issued
# receipt PDFs sitting in the tree as untracked files, one `git add -A` away
# from being published.
#
# Anchoring is not decoration. Written as a bare `storage/` this also matched
# apps/api/src/services/storage/ and silently excluded that module's source
# from every commit — the files existed locally, so everything passed here and
# only CI saw the missing module.
/storage/
/apps/api/storage/

.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# Database dumps. Anchored for the same reason storage/ is: a bare `backups/`
# would also match any source directory of that name. These contain every
# receipt the government has issued and must never reach a repository.
/backups/
/apps/api/backups/
scratch/
